## Flags for the VM of the release (docs/server-artifact.md).

## File names and the command line are UTF-8, whatever the locale.
+fnu

## No Erlang distribution: no port mapper, no listening port.
-start_epmd false

## stdout and stdin are the MCP stream. No break handler, so SIGINT ends the
## server instead of printing the BREAK menu on stdout and reading an answer
## from stdin; and no shell or other reader of stdin but the server's own.
+Bd
-noinput

## stdout is the MCP stream: the default log handler writes to stderr from the
## moment the VM boots, before any application starts (the quotes keep the
## "#" from starting a comment). config/config.exs does the same for Elixir's
## Logger, which takes the handler over when it starts.
-kernel logger '[{handler,default,logger_std_h,#{config=>#{type=>standard_error}}}]'
